oving to a paid offering | Hashnode\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.json\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"3\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"4\",{\"rel\":\"alternate\",\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"href\":\"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access.md\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering | Hashnode\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:site_name\",\"content\":\"Hashnode\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access/opengraph-image?f5676042408be5fa\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"property\":\"og:image:type\",\"content\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"property\":\"og:image:width\",\"content\":\"1200\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"property\":\"og:image:height\",\"content\":\"630\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"property\":\"og:image:alt\",\"content\":\"Changelog entry\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering | Hashnode\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access/opengraph-image?f5676042408be5fa\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:alt\",\"content\":\"Changelog entry\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"19\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:type\",\"content\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"20\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:width\",\"content\":\"1200\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"21\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:height\",\"content\":\"630\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"22\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico?favicon.3w5ba4as-0fdh.ico\",\"sizes\":\"48x48\",\"type\":\"image/x-icon\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"23\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/icon0.svg?icon0.34f3dxluhr8pt.svg\",\"sizes\":\"any\",\"type\":\"image/svg+xml\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"24\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/icon1.png?icon1.1qvf-tdx3j4n6.png\",\"sizes\":\"96x96\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"25\",{\"rel\":\"apple-touch-icon\",\"href\":\"/apple-icon.png?apple-icon.23nnv7gka9h2i.png\",\"sizes\":\"180x180\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"$L4b\",\"26\",{}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4c:\"ChangelogContent\"\n4d:I[618511,[\"$1\",\"$2\",\"$3\",\"$4\",\"$5\",\"$6\",\"$7\",\"$8\",\"$9\",\"$a\",\"$b\",\"$3a\",\"$3b\"],\"$4c\"]\n4f:I[175058,[\"$1\",\"$2\",\"$3\",\"$4\",\"$5\",\"$6\",\"$7\",\"$8\",\"$9\",\"$a\",\"$b\",\"$3a\",\"$3b\"],\"ChangelogList\"]\n48:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 text-small text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://x.com/IpseetaP\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"flex size-8 items-center justify-center rounded-md transition-colors hover:bg-accent hover:text-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"i\",null,{\"className\":\"fa-brands fa-x-twitter\",\"aria-hidden\":true}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sr-only\",\"children\":[\"Ipseeta Priyadarshini\",\" on X\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ipseeta-priyadarshini-689aa482\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"flex size-8 items-center justify-center rounded-md transition-colors hover:bg-accent hover:text-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"i\",null,{\"className\":\"fa-brands fa-linkedin\",\"aria-hidden\":true}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sr-only\",\"children\":[\"Ipseeta Priyadarshini\",\" on LinkedIn\"]}]]}]]}]\n4e:T44f,We're retiring free GraphQL API access. Every API request, queries and mutations, now requires a Pro plan on your publication.\n\n### Why we're doing this\n\nScrapers and spammers were abusing the free API at scale. Read traffic was being used to mirror posts on spam farms. Write traffic was flooding the feed with junk. Both hurt real writers on Hashnode. A small fee filters out abuse and keeps the API usable for everyone.\n\n### What changed\n\nReads used to be free. They aren't anymore. Queries against your publication now require Pro, the same as publishing.\n\n### How access works now\n\nUpgrading is self-serve. Open your blog dashboard, go to **Billing**, and click **Upgrade to Pro**. Pricing is seat-based and adjusts automatically as members join or leave. You'll see the exact monthly total on the Billing page before you check out.\n\nOnce checkout succeeds, your publication is allow-listed automatically and the API works right away. No waiting on us, no manual onboarding.\n\n### Need help?\n\nEmail [hello@hashnode.com](mailto:hello@hashnode.com) and we'll be happy to assist with your subscription.49:[\"$\",\"$L4d\",null,{\"content\":\"$4e\",\"className\":\"pt-3\"}]\n50:T871,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"Citation tracking starts with ten empty slots. Which questions do you ask? Most people type one and stop.\n\nNow you don't have to start from nothing.\n\n## Suggested queries\n\nGo to your **dashboard**, open **AEO**, then the **AI citations** tab. Click **Suggest from my articles**.\n\nWe read your articles and propose up to three questions your readers might ask an AI assistant. They save right away. Delete the ones you don't want.\n\nThe button shows while you track fewer than three queries. It's a starting point; after that, you write your own. Every query runs against ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Perplexity each day.\n\n![Suggest from my articles button on the AI citations tab](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/e3807408-b890-4bcb-85bb-4851eb168f34.png align=\"center\")\n\nAdding and removing queries saves as you click too. There is no Save button to forget.\n\n## AI traffic, one tab over\n\nIt now has its own tab in **AEO**, next to AI crawlers, Freshness queue, and AI citations.\n\nYou get a 30-day total, the trend against the previous 30 days, a daily chart, and a breakdown by assistant.\n\n![AI traffic tab in the AEO dashboard, shown with sample data](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/d1a76443-d6ba-4873-b4c8-5aad13079866.png align=\"center\")\n\nSuggested queries and the AI traffic tab are part of the Growth Plan.\n\n## See where you stand before you upgrade\n\nIf your publication isn't on the Growth Plan, the AEO page used to show a feature list. Now it shows your own numbers. You get your average AEO score, how many articles have no FAQ, how many have no question headings, and how many haven't been updated in a year.\n\n![AEO page showing a publication's own numbers](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/77c1a6b2-fe5e-45f5-ba8d-e1749210d3a6.png align=\"center\")\n\nThe editor shows them too. Open **Publish**, then **Discovery**, and look at the AEO score and FAQ sections.\n\n![AEO score and FAQ sections in the editor](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/f55b4e2a-b33f-4158-bffa-2be69499fdeb.png align=\"center\")\n\nOnly owners and admins see the numbers."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"51:T83f,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"You write in markdown. Publishing meant opening the editor and pasting it in. The Hashnode CLI cuts that to one command. Install it, log in through your browser, and publish a file straight from your terminal.\n\n![Terminal showing hashnode login printing a code](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/f2aeca97-ec46-477c-87a1-2228313fd89e.png align=\"center\")\n\nThe CLI needs a **Pro plan** on the publication, and Node.js 20 or later.\n\n## How to log in\n\nInstall it with npm, then run `hashnode login`. It prints a code and opens your browser. Type the code on the page and allow access. There is no token to copy.\n\n```plaintext\nnpm install -g @hashnode/cli\nhashnode login\n```\n\n![The page where you type the code from your terminal](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/75a9b625-3236-44be-ac83-1a4b7cc7838b.png align=\"center\")\n\nA script, a CI job, or a coding agent has no browser. Set `HASHNODE_PAT` to a Personal Access Token from Settings, Developer instead.\n\n## How to publish a post\n\nFind your publication id first:\n\n```plaintext\nhashnode --host blog.example.com publication get\n```\n\nThen publish a markdown file with one command:\n\n```plaintext\nhashnode -p \u003cid\u003e post create --title \"Hello\" --content-file post.md --tag java --tag javascript\n```\n\n![Terminal output after publishing a post](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/e4e96138-310d-4d13-bf54-48ff32566ed7.png align=\"center\")\n\nYou get the link back. Want a look before it goes live? Save a draft with `draft create`, then run `draft publish`. Upload a cover with `image upload`. Add `--json` to any command when a script needs to parse the output.\n\n## Where can I see my logins\n\nEvery login shows up under Connected apps in Developer Settings. Disconnect one and the CLI stops working at once. To end the login from your terminal, run `hashnode logout`.\n\n![Connected apps in Developer Settings listing Hashnode CLI](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/gql/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/dce0149c-f00b-41d6-ba81-911e8b7a5859.png align=\"center\")\n\nRun `hashnode --help` to see every command."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"52:T446,MCP connect links any MCP client directly to your Hashnode publications. Point one at the server below, approve the connection, and it can create, read, update, list, and delete posts, the same actions you'd take in the editor.\n\n![](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/covers/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/adfb4332-1714-4ec9-abc9-c9e23d2aa9ff.png align=\"center\")\n\nCreating, updating, listing, and deleting require a **Pro plan**.\n\n## How to connect a client\n\nPoint any MCP client at this URL to start. Claude Code, Cursor, ChatGPT, and anything else that speaks MCP can add it the same way.\n\n`https://mcp.hashnode.com/mcp`\n\nFor example, adding it in Claude Code:\n\n```plaintext\nclaude mcp add --transport http hashnode-mcp https://mcp.hashnode.com/mcp\n```\n\n## Where can I see the connected apps\n\nEvery connected app shows up in Developer Settings. Disconnect any one without touching the others. Access cuts off immediately.\n\n![](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/covers/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/55fd373c-2ebb-4659-9b01-b2e107239803.png align=\"center\")\n\nThis is v1. More tools and permissions are coming.53:T6ef,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"AI citation tracking told you when your blog got cited. It never told you who else showed up in the same answer, or how many readers AI assistants actually send you. Now it does, in two new spots in your dashboard.\n\n## Who else gets cited\n\nGo to your **dashboard**, open **AEO**, then the **AI citations** tab. Below your tracked queries, you'll find a new panel.\n\nIt ranks every other domain that showed up in the same AI answers, sorted by how often they got cited.\n\nYour own row sits in that list too, marked \"You,\" so you can see exactly where you rank. Filter to one tracked question at a time, or leave it on the aggregate view to see who dominates across all your questions.\n\n![Who else gets cited panel on the AI citations tab](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/covers/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/3cce0b0a-4945-4712-9b32-dcfefe914c5d.png align=\"center\")\n\n## AI traffic\n\nGo to your **dashboard** and open **Analytics**. Scroll past your usual stats and you'll find a new AI traffic card.\n\nIt counts sessions where a reader arrived from ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, or Claude, the same four engines the citations tab tracks.\n\nYou get a 30-day total, a trend against the previous 30 days, a daily bar chart, and a breakdown by assistant.\n\n![AI traffic card on the Analytics page](https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/covers/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/cc9be823-a1bb-4c0e-8034-aec3944efc13.png align=\"center\")\n\nThis one needs Hashnode to render your blog. If your publication is headless, we never see the analytics, so the card stays empty. Track analytics on your own frontend instead.\n\n## Wrapping up\n\nBoth features are part of the Growth Plan. AI search is a real source of readers now, not a hypothetical one. These two features exist so you can measure it instead of guessing."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4a:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-3 pt-24\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-title-3 text-foreground\",\"children\":\"More updates\"}],[\"$\",\"$L3d\",null,{\"href\":\"/changelog\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-label text-foreground underline decoration-transparent underline-offset-3 transition-colors hover:decoration-current\",\"children\":[\"All updates\",[\"$\",\"$L3c\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"icon\":{\"name\":\"arrow-right\",\"size\":24,\"node\":[[\"path\",{\"d\":\"M5 12h14\",\"key\":\"1ays0h\"}],[\"path\",{\"d\":\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\",\"key\":\"xquz4c\"}]]},\"className\":\"inline shrink-0 align-[-0.125em] text-sm\",\"size\":\"1em\",\"strokeWidth\":1.75,\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L4f\",null,{\"entries\":[{\"id\":\"2026-10-07-aeo-suggested-queries\",\"date\":\"2026-10-07T11:28:51.842Z\",\"title\":\"AEO toolkit: Start tracking with suggested queries\",\"summary\":\"Suggested queries to start tracking, an AI traffic tab, and your own AEO numbers before you upgrade.\",\"category\":\"improvement\",\"emoji\":\"🎯\",\"coverPhoto\":\"\",\"authorId\":\"ipseeta\",\"content\":\"$50\"},{\"id\":\"2026-10-06-hashnode-cli\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T10:10:15.792Z\",\"title\":\"Hashnode CLI: Publish and manage your blog from the terminal\",\"summary\":\"Create drafts, posts, and many more from your terminal\",\"category\":\"feature\",\"emoji\":\"⌨️\",\"coverPhoto\":\"\",\"authorId\":\"ipseeta\",\"content\":\"$51\"},{\"id\":\"2026-09-22-mcp-connect\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T08:11:17.583Z\",\"title\":\"MCP connect: Give Claude, ChatGPT, or Codex read and write access to your posts\\\"\",\"summary\":\"Connect any MCP client to your Hashnode posts\",\"category\":\"feature\",\"emoji\":\"🔌\",\"coverPhoto\":\"\",\"authorId\":\"ipseeta\",\"content\":\"$52\"},{\"id\":\"2026-09-01-presigned-post-deprecated\",\"date\":\"2026-09-01T06:04:11.526Z\",\"title\":\"GraphQL image uploads: presignedPost is deprecated\",\"summary\":\"createImageUploadURL now returns presignedPut too. Switch over before presignedPost goes away.\",\"category\":\"deprecated\",\"emoji\":\"🔌\",\"coverPhoto\":\"\",\"authorId\":\"ipseeta\",\"content\":\"### For developers using our GraphQL API\\n\\n`createImageUploadURL` now returns a new `presignedPut` field alongside the existing `presignedPost`. `presignedPost` is deprecated and scheduled for removal on September 7, 2026.\\n\\nMove your integration to `presignedPut`: sign one PUT request instead of a multi-field POST, then call `confirmImageUpload(key)` once the upload finishes.\\n\\n```graphql\\nmutation {\\n  createImageUploadURL(input: { contentType: \\\"image/png\\\" }) {\\n    presignedPut { url cdnUrl key }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nPUT your image bytes to `url` with a matching `Content-Type` header, then call `confirmImageUpload(input: { key: key })` and use the returned `cdnUrl`.\\n\\nIf you use `gql-skill` or the `publish-github-action`, update to the latest version before the removal date.\"},{\"id\":\"2026-08-25-aeo-citations-and-traffic\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T13:16:02.227Z\",\"title\":\"AEO toolkit: See who else gets cited, and how much traffic AI sends you\",\"summary\":\"Growth Plan gets two more features: see who else gets cited, and see how many readers AI sends you.\",\"category\":\"feature\",\"emoji\":\"👀\",\"coverPhoto\":\"\",\"authorId\":\"ipseeta\",\"content\":\"$53\"}],\"authors\":{\"ipseeta\":{\"name\":\"Ipseeta Priyadarshini\",\"photo\":\"https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/avatars/54d750ac3adc13883c24a9be/3093eee5-6409-49a3-9b2b-fa52b59f7227.jpg\",\"profileUrl\":\"https://hashnode.com/@ipseeta\",\"x\":\"https://x.com/IpseetaP\",\"linkedin\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ipseeta-priyadarshini-689aa482\"},\"fazlerocks\":{\"name\":\"Syed Fazle Rahman\",\"photo\":\"https://cdn.hashnode.com/uploads/avatars/54b81b237393d8e81463c55c/2ed271c5-c71f-4678-a8ce-22c4bea1b4eb.jpg\",\"profileUrl\":\"https://hashnode.com/@fazlerocks\",\"x\":\"https://twitter.com/fazlerocks\",\"linkedin\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/fazlerocks/\"},\"sandeep\":{\"name\":\"Sandeep Panda\",\"photo\":\"https://cdn.hashnode.com/res/hashnode/image/upload/v1692169982147/T8HXgPnnf.png\",\"profileUrl\":\"https://hashnode.com/@sandeep\",\"x\":\"http://twitter.com/sandeepg33k\",\"linkedin\":\"\"}},\"variant\":\"compact\"}]]}]\n"])</script><title>GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering | Hashnode</title><meta name="description" content="Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard."/><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json"/><link rel="canonical" href="https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access"/><link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access.md"/><meta property="og:title" content="GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering | Hashnode"/><meta property="og:description" content="Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard."/><meta property="og:url" content="https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access"/><meta property="og:site_name" content="Hashnode"/><meta property="og:image" content="https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access/opengraph-image?f5676042408be5fa"/><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"/><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"/><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"/><meta property="og:image:alt" content="Changelog entry"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering | Hashnode"/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access/opengraph-image?f5676042408be5fa"/><meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="Changelog entry"/><meta name="twitter:image:type" content="image/png"/><meta name="twitter:image:width" content="1200"/><meta name="twitter:image:height" content="630"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico?favicon.3w5ba4as-0fdh.ico" sizes="48x48" type="image/x-icon"/><link rel="icon" href="/icon0.svg?icon0.34f3dxluhr8pt.svg" sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml"/><link rel="icon" href="/icon1.png?icon1.1qvf-tdx3j4n6.png" sizes="96x96" type="image/png"/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-icon.png?apple-icon.23nnv7gka9h2i.png" sizes="180x180" type="image/png"/><script>document.querySelectorAll('body link[rel="icon"], body link[rel="apple-touch-icon"]').forEach(el => document.head.appendChild(el))</script><div hidden id="S:2"><main class="flex flex-1 min-h-0 flex-col"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://hashnode.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Changelog","item":"https://hashnode.com/changelog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering","description":"Free GraphQL API access is retired. Reading and publishing both require a Pro plan you can upgrade to from your blog dashboard.","url":"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access","datePublished":"2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z","dateModified":"2026-05-13T00:00:00.000Z","about":{"@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Hashnode","url":"https://hashnode.com"},"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Ipseeta Priyadarshini","url":"https://hashnode.com"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Hashnode","url":"https://hashnode.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://hashnode.com/web-app-manifest-192x192.png","width":192,"height":192}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://hashnode.com/changelog/2026-05-13-graphql-api-paid-access"}}</script><div class="sticky top-0 z-20 h-13 shrink-0 items-center gap-3 bar-rule bg-background/80 px-4 backdrop-blur sm:px-6 hidden sm:flex"><span class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-2"><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2.5 text-label text-foreground transition-colors h-7 bg-muted hover:bg-accent" href="/changelog"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-left inline shrink-0 align-[-0.125em] text-sm" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path><path d="M19 12H5"></path></svg>All updates</a><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-input">/</span></span><div class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-title-4 text-foreground">GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering</div></div><section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-184 px-5 pb-20 sm:px-8"><div class="-mx-5 flex h-12 items-center border-b border-border px-5 sm:hidden"><a class="inline-flex h-8 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md bg-muted px-2.5 text-label text-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-accent hover:no-underline" href="/changelog"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-left inline shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path><path d="M19 12H5"></path></svg><span>All updates</span></a></div><article class="pt-6 sm:pt-14"><header class="flex flex-col gap-5 border-b border-border pb-8"><span class="flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center size-13 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card text-title-2 shadow-sm sm:size-16 sm:text-title-2"><span role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="leading-none">🔌</span></span><div class="flex flex-col gap-3"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1"><span data-slot="badge" data-variant="secondary" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-5.5 rounded-full border border-transparent px-2 text-caption w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-secondary/90 bg-muted text-foreground">Deprecated</span><time dateTime="2026-05-13" class="text-meta text-muted-foreground">May 13, 2026</time></div><h1 class="text-article-title text-balance text-foreground">GraphQL API is moving to a paid offering</h1></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3"><a href="https://hashnode.com/@ipseeta" class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2.5 text-meta text-foreground hover:underline"><span data-slot="avatar" class="relative flex shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-full size-7"><span data-slot="avatar-fallback" class="bg-muted flex size-full items-center justify-center rounded-full text-caption">I</span></span><span class="truncate">Ipseeta Priyadarshini</span></a><span class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 text-small text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://x.com/IpseetaP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex size-8 items-center justify-center rounded-md transition-colors hover:bg-accent hover:text-foreground"><i class="fa-brands fa-x-twitter" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="sr-only">Ipseeta Priyadarshini<!-- --> on X</span></a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ipseeta-priyadarshini-689aa482" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex size-8 items-center justify-center rounded-md transition-colors hover:bg-accent hover:text-foreground"><i class="fa-brands fa-linkedin" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="sr-only">Ipseeta Priyadarshini<!-- --> on LinkedIn</span></a></span></div></header><div class="prose prose-reading dark:prose-invert max-w-none [&amp;_h2]:pt-5 pt-3"><p>We&#x27;re retiring free GraphQL API access. Every API request, queries and mutations, now requires a Pro plan on your publication.</p>
<h3>Why we&#x27;re doing this</h3>
<p>Scrapers and spammers were abusing the free API at scale. Read traffic was being used to mirror posts on spam farms. Write traffic was flooding the feed with junk. Both hurt real writers on Hashnode. A small fee filters out abuse and keeps the API usable for everyone.</p>
<h3>What changed</h3>
<p>Reads used to be free. They aren&#x27;t anymore. Queries against your publication now require Pro, the same as publishing.</p>
<h3>How access works now</h3>
<p>Upgrading is self-serve. Open your blog dashboard, go to <strong>Billing</strong>, and click <strong>Upgrade to Pro</strong>. Pricing is seat-based and adjusts automatically as members join or leave. You&#x27;ll see the exact monthly total on the Billing page before you check out.</p>
<p>Once checkout succeeds, your publication is allow-listed automatically and the API works right away. No waiting on us, no manual onboarding.</p>
<h3>Need help?</h3>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@hashnode.com">hello@hashnode.com</a> and we&#x27;ll be happy to assist with your subscription.</p></div></article><div class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-24"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3"><h2 class="text-title-3 text-foreground">More updates</h2><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-label text-foreground underline decoration-transparent underline-offset-3 transition-colors hover:decoration-current" href="/changelog">All updates<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right inline shrink-0 align-[-0.125em] text-sm" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div><div class="divide-y divide-border"><a class="group flex h-16 items-center gap-3.5 hover:no-underline" href="/changelog/2026-10-07-aeo-suggested-queries"><span class="flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center size-8 rounded-md bg-muted text-body"><span role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="leading-none">🎯</span></span><span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-title-4 text-foreground"><span class="underline decoration-transparent decoration-1 underline-offset-4 transition-colors group-hover:decoration-current">AEO toolkit: Start tracking with suggested queries</span></span><span data-slot="badge" data-variant="secondary" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-5.5 rounded-full border border-transparent px-2 text-caption w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-secondary/90 bg-muted text-foreground">Improvement</span><time dateTime="2026-1